    <item>
      <title>5.1. For loops</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.1.-for-loops/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.1.-for-loops/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;51-for-loops&#34;&gt;5.1. For loops&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#51-for-loops&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For loops are the most common loops in Swift, and you&amp;rsquo;ll probably use this loop for more than 90% of cases. We use &lt;code&gt;for&lt;/code&gt; loops to iterate over a sequence of values or a range of values.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For example, the following code prints the integers in the range &lt;code&gt;1...10&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; range = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;..&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; number &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; range{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(number)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another example could be iterating through an array and printing the elements:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>5.2. While loops</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.2.-while-loops/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.2.-while-loops/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;52-while-loops&#34;&gt;5.2. While loops&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#52-while-loops&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The second most common loops in Swift are &lt;code&gt;while&lt;/code&gt; loops. We use a while loop to run a code block repeatedly as long as a given condition is true. A general structure of a &lt;code&gt;while&lt;/code&gt; loop is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; condition {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//code block&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For example, the following code prints all the integers below 50:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; targetNum = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; targetNum &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//code block&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(targetNum)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    targetNum &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here the condition is: if &lt;code&gt;targetNum&lt;/code&gt; is less than or equal to 50.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>5.3. Repeat loops</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.3.-repeat-loops/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.3.-repeat-loops/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;53-repeat-loops&#34;&gt;5.3. Repeat loops&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#53-repeat-loops&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The third way of writing loops is &lt;code&gt;repeat&lt;/code&gt; loops. It is identical to a while loop, but the condition is checked at the end of the code block. If we use the same example from before, we can write:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; myNum = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;repeat&lt;/span&gt;{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//code block&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(myNum)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    myNum &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;} &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; myNum &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The point is &lt;code&gt;repeat&lt;/code&gt; loops will execute the code block at least once. So, you should be careful about the cases where the first iteration may result in errors.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>5.4. Break and continue</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.4.-break-and-continue/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/02-swift-fundamentals/loops/5.4.-break-and-continue/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;54-break-and-continue&#34;&gt;5.4. Break and continue&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#54-break-and-continue&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;breakingexiting-loops&#34;&gt;Breaking/exiting loops&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#breakingexiting-loops&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Sometimes we want to stop repeating the code block in a loop. We use the keyword &lt;code&gt;break&lt;/code&gt; to do that. Let&amp;rsquo;s look into the example below:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; breakPoint = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; countDown = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; breakPoint &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;I will run!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//  activating break point&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; countDown == breakPoint{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;I am tired now!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;break&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    countDown &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here the while loop is running infinitely if the value of &lt;code&gt;breakPoint&lt;/code&gt; is greater than or equal to &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;. So, we need to break it when the &lt;code&gt;countDown&lt;/code&gt; reaches the &lt;code&gt;breakPoint&lt;/code&gt;. Thats where we user the keyword &lt;code&gt;break&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
